// Title: Cloudflared Tunnel Connections Cleanup
// Sigma ID: 7050bba1-1aed-454e-8f73-3f46f09ce56a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-17 | Modified: 2023-12-21
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1102, T1090, T1572
// Description: Detects execution of the "cloudflared" tool with the tunnel "cleanup" flag in order to cleanup
//   tunnel connections.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of Cloudflared.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared
//   - https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-apps
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cloudflared_tunnel_cleanup.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " tunnel " and ProcessCommandLine contains "cleanup ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-config " or ProcessCommandLine contains "-connector-id ")
